---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '@/components/Container.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';

const title = "Essential Apps — Travel Guide";
const description = "The digital tools and local messaging standards you need to set up before your journey begins.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": title,
  "description": description,
  "url": `${SITE.url}/guides/essential-apps`
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="py-20 lg:py-32">
    <Container>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <nav class="mb-12">
          <a href="/guides" class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors">
            ← All guides
          </a>
        </nav>

        <header class="mb-16">
          <span class="eyebrow mb-4 inline-block">Chapter 01</span>
          <h1 class="text-h1 font-serif font-light mb-8">Essential Digital Tools</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
            Modern travel relies on a small constellation of digital tools. Setting these up before you hit the terminal ensures a seamless transition upon arrival.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

          <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mt-16 mb-8">Navigation & Transport</h2>
          <p>Beyond Google Maps, ensure you have the local ride-sharing equivalents registered and verified. Standards shift drastically once you cross borders:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Southeast Asia:</strong> Grab is the dominant layer for both transit and food delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>South Korea:</strong> KakaoTaxi is essential, as Google Maps functionality is limited.</li>
            <li><strong>Europe:</strong> Bolt and Uber share the market across most major capitals.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="bg-surface p-8 border border-border my-12">
            <p class="text-sm font-sans italic text-muted-foreground m-0">
              <strong class="text-primary not-italic">Technical Note:</strong> Download offline maps for your destination city to save data and battery during the critical first hours of arrival.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mt-16 mb-8">Messaging & Local Logic</h2>
          <p>International messaging standards vary. Relying on SMS is often unreliable and expensive. Install the primary communication layer for your region:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> The default for most of Europe, South America, and Africa.</li>
            <li><strong>Line:</strong> Essential for Japan, Taiwan, and Thailand.</li>
            <li><strong>Signal:</strong> Recommended for privacy-conscious routing.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mt-16 mb-8">Language & Translation</h2>
          <p>Google Translate with offline language packs is your baseline. However, for high-fidelity translation in formal settings or menu deciphering, specialized tools often perform better.</p>
          <p>Apps like <strong>DeepL</strong> provide superior nuance for European languages, while <strong>Papago</strong> is unmatched for Korean and Japanese context.</p>
        </div>

        <footer class="mt-20 pt-20 border-t border-border flex justify-between items-center">
          <div class="flex flex-col">
            <span class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground mb-2">Next</span>
            <a href="/guides/visa-entry" class="text-xl font-serif hover:text-primary transition-colors">Visa & Entry Information →</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
